Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat(openobserve): fixed-width canonical hex trace and
 span ids

Carries over openobserve/browser-sdk#25 (commit 40443a4a2), which was made
directly on the openobserve branch and so was not in the patch series:

- RUM event fields _o2.trace_id and _o2.span_id (resource events) use
  fixed-width hex (32 and 16 chars). BigInt toString(16) drops leading zeros
  and UUIDv7 trace ids always start with a zero nibble, so the stored id never
  matched the 32-char trace_id of the traces stream.
- x-openobserve-* propagator headers follow the backend contract
  (get_or_create_trace_id): x-openobserve-span-id (was -parent-id) and padded
  hex values instead of decimal.
- new toPaddedTraceIdHex / toPaddedSpanIdHex helpers; the width-guessing
  toPaddedHexadecimalString is kept for b3 only.

Specs updated as in the original change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
